      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would be a super fun way to show off achievements from worlds.\n\nI imagine this feeling similar to steam's \"achievement showcase\" block you can put on your profile, where you'd amass badges given from worlds and be able to display a few directly on your profile. I agree it'd be cool to put them on your nameplate too! Sorta like Splatoon's nametag badges.\n\nObviously you'd need to consider how to avoid the system being abused without stressing too hard about moderation, so I think a system similar to the way Twitch grants streamers custom emote slots based on their sub count could work pretty well. World creators could be granted custom badges to award to players based on their trust rank, world visits, etc.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-04-11T17:43:55.898Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So currently, the badges part of the profile is pretty empty.\n\nI Suggest that the ability for world and group creators to add custom badges is added.\n\nPeople could get new badges for example by :\n\n- Visiting a world\n\n- Doing something in a world (triggered by Udon Graph/Udon Sharp)\n\n- Being part of a group\n\n- Having a certain role in the group\n\n- Others\n\nLet creators decide how the badges will be acquired.\n\nAlso, one more new use for the badges could be the ability to put them on the group banner above your head. \n\nMaybe being able to select where exactly it will be put on the banner, like a sticker.",
